---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { config } from '../config';
---

<Base title="Express Install Service Terms" description="Plain-language terms for the Express Install service: what is included, how we handle access and security, and our refund policy.">
  <main id="main" class="mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl flex-1 px-4 py-8">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Service terms' }]} />
    <h1 class="mt-6 text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-900">Express Install: Service terms</h1>
    <div class="prose-lite text-slate-700">
      <p>This page explains the {config.express.productName} service in plain language. It is a template that should be reviewed by a qualified professional before you rely on it.</p>

      <h2>What you get</h2>
      <p>The price is a one-time ${config.express.priceUsd}. {config.service.scope}</p>

      <h2>What is not included</h2>
      <p>{config.service.outOfScope}</p>

      <h2>Turnaround</h2>
      <p>We aim to finish {config.express.turnaroundText} after we receive the details and access we need from you. Delays caused by missing access, unavailable accounts or third-party outages can extend this.</p>

      <h2>Access and security</h2>
      <p>{config.service.accessMethods}</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Only share access through a collaborator, staff or invite system. Do not send passwords by email or chat.</li>
        <li>We only use access for the job you paid for.</li>
        <li>You can remove our access when the job is done, and we recommend you do.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>After delivery</h2>
      <p>{config.service.revisions}</p>

      <h2>Refunds</h2>
      <p>{config.service.refundPolicy}</p>

      <h2>Your responsibilities</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Make sure you have the right to give us access to the accounts involved.</li>
        <li>Keep a backup of your site or store before we start if you can.</li>
        <li>Tell us about any other tools that may conflict with the new install.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions? Email {config.supportEmail}.</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: {config.legal.lastUpdated}. Operated by {config.legal.companyName}.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
